<div class="page">
    <div class="two-column-layout">
        <div class="column">
            <div class="content-section">
                <div class="section-heading">PART 1</div>
                <h2 style="font-size: 16pt; font-weight: normal;">PREPARING FOR YOUR ARRIVAL</h2>
                <p><strong>WELCOME TO AUC!</strong></p>
                <p>We know you have a lot on your mind as you prepare to start your MD degree, so the information in this Welcome Guide is designed to help make this a smooth transition.</p>
                <p>Be sure to read everything on these pages and then complete the necessary tasks.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="column">
            <div class="card">
                <div class="section-heading">TRAVEL DOCUMENTATION</div>
                <p>You will need to travel with the following documents:</p>
                <div class="list-item"><input type="checkbox"> Valid passport (check that your passport is signed and has not expired)</div>
                <div class="list-item"><input type="checkbox"> AUC School of Medicine acceptance letter</div>
                <div class="list-item"><input type="checkbox"> Naturalized U.S. citizens must show an original naturalization certificate with photo ID</div>
                <div class="list-item"><input type="checkbox"> Permanent U.S. residents must travel with their permanent resident card (green card) and valid passport</div>
                <p><strong>If you plan to bring a spouse or other family members:</strong></p>
                <div class="list-item"><input type="checkbox"> Marriage certificate</div>
                <div class="list-item"><input type="checkbox"> Return tickets</div>
                <p style="margin-top: 15px;"><strong>NOTE:</strong> If you are not a U.S. or Canadian citizen, you may be required to obtain a visa. Please contact the nearest Dutch embassy/consulate to find out if you need a visa or other documentation. Our immigration coordinator will be in contact with you to get any appropriate information and will request a landing permit on your behalf if needed. Once you receive the permit, you will be able to meet with the embassy to obtain a visa for your stay in Sint Maarten.</p>
                <p>For more information on travel to Sint Maarten, please visit the official <a href="#">Sint Maarten website</a> at <span data-field="sint_maarten_url">{{ sint_maarten_url }}</span></p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="footer">
        <div class="page-identifier">AUC SCHOOL OF MEDICINE</div>
        <div class="page-number">8</div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
    <div class="two-column-layout">
        <div class="column">
            <div class="content-section">
                <div class="section-heading">PLANNING YOUR JOURNEY TO SINT MAARTEN</div>
                <p>AUC's medical sciences campus is located in Sint Maarten, a 37-square-mile Caribbean island approximately 150 miles east of Puerto Rico. The island is shared by the governments of France and the Netherlands and, as a result, boasts a vibrant blend of both cultures. Students can easily navigate the island, as English is spoken everywhere and the U.S. dollar is generally accepted. With no shortage of cuisines, nationalities (estimated at over 100), and world-renowned tourism spots, Sint Maarten makes for an exciting environment for living and learning.</p>
                <div class="sub-heading">SCHEDULING YOUR FLIGHT</div>
                <p>Princess Juliana International Airport (SXM), Sint Maarten's main airport, is a major Caribbean hub for U.S. and Canadian airlines and welcomes direct flights from several North American cities.</p>
                <p>Upon arrival, students can take a two-mile taxi ride to AUC's campus for about $20 USD. During orientation week, we will have a welcome team on-site to greet you at the airport and escort you to campus via our complimentary shuttle service. We encourage students to align their travel with the orientation dates to use this service. Please visit: <a href="http://aucmed.edu/about/Events/Welcome-Week.html">aucmed.edu/about/Events/Welcome-Week.html</a></p>
                <div class="sub-heading">VIRTUAL CAMPUS TOUR</div>
                <p>Explore before you go. Take a self-guided 360-degree virtual tour of our campus: <a href="http://aucmed.edu/about/virtual-tour">aucmed.edu/about/virtual-tour</a></p>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="column">
            <div class="content-section">
                <div class="section-heading">INTERNATIONAL TRAVEL REGISTRATION</div>
                <p>Students and their families are encouraged to register their travel with their home country's department of state or foreign affairs. This will ensure that local embassies and consulates are aware of your extended stay in Sint Maarten and can communicate with you in the case of an emergency, or should your passport be lost or stolen.</p>
                <p>Two popular services are the United States' Smart Traveler Enrollment Program (STEP) and Canada's Registration of Canadians Abroad. Please check with your home country for registration availability.</p>
                <div class="sub-heading">RELOCATING A FAMILY</div>
                <p>AUC School of Medicine extends a warm welcome to partners and family members who are relocating to Sint Maarten with a student. The AUC Spokes Organization is the foremost resource for families and serves as a major social network and support system before and during your time on island. Get advice ahead of your move and connect with other families who have already transitioned to island life. The Spokes Organization is here to foster fellowship and community involvement for your loved ones while they are on the island (and you are in the classroom). For further information, please visit: <a href="#">aucspokesorg@gmail.com</a></p>
                <div class="sub-heading">CONTACT US</div>
                <p>Or contact them directly at: <a href="mailto:aucspokesorg@gmail.com">aucspokesorg@gmail.com</a></p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="footer">
        <div class="page-identifier">AUC SCHOOL OF MEDICINE</div>
        <div class="page-number">9</div>
    </div>
</div>

