                <div class="section-heading">WHAT TO BRING TO SINT MAARTEN</div>
                <div style="display: flex; gap: 40px;">
                    <div style="flex: 1;">
                        <div class="sub-heading">TECHNOLOGY</div>
                        <ul class="list-item"><li>A laptop and optionally a tablet, set up with a cloud backup service such as Box or Dropbox to protect critical data</li></ul>
                        <ul class="list-item"><li>Grounded power strips (ensure they have surge protection)</li></ul>
                        <ul class="list-item"><li>USB drive</li></ul>
                        <ul class="list-item"><li>Unlocked cell phone (for those who want to purchase an island SIM card; not needed for residents of AUC on campus housing)</li></ul>
                        <ul class="list-item"><li>Microsoft Office Suite*</li></ul>
                        <p style="font-size: 9pt; margin-top: 10px;">*Note: Students receive a license to Microsoft Office Suite free of charge. After receiving notification that your AUC account has been activated, please log in to the portal to find information on how to access your license. It should arrive by the following day.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div style="flex: 1;">
                        <div class="sub-heading">CLOTHING</div>
                        <ul class="list-item"><li>Leisure/Everyday Wear: Shorts, tank tops, flip-flops, running shoes, and slides</li></ul>
                        <ul class="list-item"><li>Sweaters and long-sleeved shirts for lecture halls and study rooms</li></ul>
                        <ul class="list-item"><li>2-3 bathing suits</li></ul>
                        <ul class="list-item"><li>Raincoat, hat for sun protection, and sunglasses</li></ul>
                        <div class="sub-heading">MEDICATIONS</div>
                        <p>If you take medications, bring enough to last the entire semester. Please contact a Sint Maarten pharmacist to ensure your medications are available on the island.</p>
                        <p style="margin-top: 15px;"><strong><span data-field="pharmacy_contact">{{ pharmacy_contact }}</span></strong><br>
                        +1 721-545-3200</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
