<div class="page">
    <div class="two-column-layout">
        <div class="column">
            <div class="content-section">
                <div class="section-heading">GETTING STARTED: NEW STUDENT TASKS</div>
                <p>As a new student, there are a few things you need to complete.</p>
                <div class="sub-heading">MY AUC MED</div>
                <p>The My AUC Med student portal is a central information hub for AUC students. Please familiarize yourself with the resources available here: <a href="http://community.aucmed.edu">community.aucmed.edu</a></p>
                <div class="sub-heading">YOUR AUC EMAIL</div>
                <p>Your AUC email account will be used for all official notices and communication with the institution. Web email is accessible through <a href="http://outlook.com/students">outlook.com/students</a>.</p>
                <div class="sub-heading">HEALTH INSURANCE</div>
                <p>Students are required to obtain global health insurance coverage through our sponsored provider, Nagico. You will be automatically enrolled upon your acceptance to AUC and will receive your insurance card during New Student Orientation Week. Please note that if you have a dependent or significant other can purchase additional insurance. You can speak with a Nagico agent during Orientation Week.</p>
                <p>AUC students who do not have health insurance coverage will not receive temporary residency permit. Please be sure to keep your primary health insurance until the first day of class to avoid any disruption in coverage.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="column">
            <div class="content-section">
                <div class="section-heading">GET CONNECTED</div>
                <p>Every incoming class at AUC is assigned a Facebook group where students can connect and post updates about various school and outside activities. Please join your class Facebook group to receive an email to join the Facebook group. Student clubs and organizations are also active on Facebook.</p>
                <div class="sub-heading">APPS TO DOWNLOAD</div>
                <p>The following applications are used regularly among students and on the island. We recommend downloading them before you arrive.</p>
                <div style="display: flex; gap: 20px; margin-top: 15px;">
                    <div style="flex: 1;">
                        <p><strong>VENMO</strong></p>
                        <p>Venmo is a digital wallet application. Send and receive payments with a Venmo account using money you have in Venmo, or link your bank account or debit card quickly. Some students choose to use it as a convenient way to pay club dues, buy swag and supplies on campus, or make other purchases.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div style="flex: 1;">
                        <p><strong>WHATSAPP</strong></p>
                        <p>WhatsApp is a messaging and calling application that allows users to securely send text, photos, audio, and video all over the world.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
