            <h3 style="font-size: 16pt;">CURRENCY</h3>
            <p style="font-size: 11pt;">The U.S. dollar is widely accepted throughout the island. However, U.S. personal checks are usually not accepted. We advise students to travel with an ATM card and/or a sufficient amount of cash to support them during the first few weeks of school. If you have not made housing accommodations, be prepared to have months' rent in cash available for your off-campus security deposit.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="width: 48%;">
            <h3 style="font-size: 16pt;">MAIL & PACKAGES</h3>
            <p style="font-size: 11pt;">AUC receives packages and mail from various carriers, including USPS, Canada Post, UPS, DHL, and FedEx. Regular mail (USPS) takes six to eight weeks, and express mail can take up to 10 days. Courier services take two or three days for delivery. Students should ship to the AUC School of Medicine, <span data-field="mailing_address">{{ mailing_address }}</span>. Once you arrive in Sint Maarten, you can set up a local mailbox through the island's mail service. Mail is distributed to campus every Monday and Thursday and will be delivered to our Notes Service. Students will receive an email alert when a package arrives.</p>
