        <div style="width: 48%;">
            <h3 style="font-size: 16pt;">BANKING</h3>
            <p style="font-size: 11pt;">There are several banks on the island: Republic Financial Holdings Limited (RFHL), Royal Bank of Canada (RBC Caribbean), Oran Bank N.V., and Windward Islands Bank. If you require a local account, we suggest opening a non-resident U.S. dollar savings account. You will need to have your passport, acceptance letter, and a minimum balance of $250-$500. To open a checking or savings account, you will need a letter of reference from your current bank, along with your passport and a minimum balance. Please be aware that checking accounts are expensive to maintain and checks are not readily accepted by merchants. However, ATMs are available for both checking and savings accounts.</p>
            <p style="font-size: 11pt;">Student credit balances are issued in U.S. dollars, and students may receive their bank credit directly by deposit to a U.S. bank account or a U.S. check mailed to their home address. Students may also opt to pick up a check on campus.</p>
            <p style="font-size: 11pt;">Note: Students should call their bank to learn about how their current accounts will operate on the island.</p>
        </div>
