    <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-top: 30px;">
        <div style="width: 48%;">
            <h3 style="font-size: 16pt;">SHIPPING, RENTING, OR PURCHASING A CAR</h3>
            <p style="font-size: 11pt;">You can buy a used car in Sint Maarten or you can ship your car to the island. For information on shipping a car, contact <span data-field="shipping_contact">{{ shipping_contact }}</span>. The typical price range for a used car is between $800 to $4,000, depending on its condition. If you plan on purchasing a used car, we strongly advise you to have it inspected by a local mechanic before you purchase it. We also advise having your selected insurance provider review all documentation prior to making any transaction to avoid purchasing a stolen vehicle.</p>
            <p style="font-size: 11pt;">You may also choose to lease a car. Leases are around $475+ per month depending on the make and model.</p>
            <p style="font-size: 11pt;">Of the car (insurance not included). Do not rush into a lease agreement; give yourself adequate time to evaluate all of your available options. We recommend signing a long-term lease agreement, as they do not have cancellation options.</p>
            <p style="font-size: 11pt;">Students can also rent a car with an agency of their choice. We recommend going through reputable agencies like Dollar/Thrifty Car Rental. Students can speak with a Dollar/Thrifty representative on campus, in the main lobby, or at the Rotunda. To rent a car, you will need to have funds for a security deposit (typically $100-$500) and a valid driver's license. Car rental fees begin around $30/day (plus tax), and liability and collision insurance are available for $8/day and $10/day each.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="width: 48%;">
            <h3 style="font-size: 16pt;">MANDATORY INSPECTIONS & INSURANCE</h3>
            <p style="font-size: 11pt;">The Sint Maarten government issues automobile stickers as a part of its road tax system. It will cost $35 to have your car inspected. The inspection will be good for one or two years depending on the type of vehicle. In addition, you will have to pay a yearly road tax of about $20. If you own a car in Sint Maarten, you will need to insure it with a local company. You cannot use your vehicle insurance from home. Annual automobile insurance can cost approximately $200-$540, and scooter insurance can cost $60-$150. Representatives from Peoples Insurance regularly visit campus to set up and renew insurance for students.</p>
            <h3 style="font-size: 16pt; margin-top: 20px;">ELECTRICITY</h3>
            <p style="font-size: 11pt;">The campus is hooked up to the local electrical grid (GEBE). AUC also has backup generators that provide electricity for the campus and university apartments. The Dutch side of the island, where AUC is located, has electrical current of 110 volts, 60 cycles, compatible with U.S. computers and small appliances. The French side of the island uses an electrical current of 220 volts, 50 cycles.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

