<div class="page">
  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-bottom: 40px;">
    <div style="flex: 1; padding-right: 20px;">
      <h2 style="font-size: 24px; margin-bottom: 20px;">CAMPUS ACCESS</h2>
      <p style="line-height: 1.6;">The <span data-field="campus_name">{{ campus_name }}</span> campus and university apartments are monitored by security personnel. The only people allowed on campus are AUC faculty, staff, students, and authorized visitors. AUC reserves the right to ask any visitor, student, or staff member to leave the facility following any disruptive behavior. Authorized visitors must check in with security and obtain a guest permit in order to access the campus. Safety and security personnel will issue students an identification badge during registration.</p>
    </div>
    <div style="flex: 1; padding-left: 20px;">
      <h2 style="font-size: 24px; margin-bottom: 20px;">CAMPUS SECURITY</h2>
      <p style="line-height: 1.6;">AUC is committed to providing a secure and crime-free campus environment. Security awareness is an important part of our culture at AUC, and we encourage all students, faculty, and staff to accept responsibility for their own safety as well as the safety of others. The AUC Office of Safety & Security provides service 24/7 and maintains ongoing communication with the police department of <span data-field="city_name">{{ city_name }}</span>. We closely monitor the campus as well as nearby residences and neighborhoods using surveillance monitoring, bike patrols, and K-9 service. We also provide a shuttle service. The Office of Safety & Security is also responsible for emergency response, campus vehicle registration, university ID badges, lost and found, and wellness checks. Please refer to the annual safety and student disclosures brochure for updated campus crime statistics as well as information on reporting procedures, appropriate conduct, and the disaster/emergency response plan.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-top: 40px;">
    <div style="flex: 1; padding-right: 20px;">
      <h2 style="font-size: 24px; margin-bottom: 20px;">AUC COMPLIMENTARY SHUTTLE SERVICE</h2>
      <p style="line-height: 1.6;">During evening hours, AUC offers a courtesy shuttle service from campus to surrounding neighborhoods (<span data-field="neighborhood_1">{{ neighborhood_1 }}</span>, <span data-field="neighborhood_2">{{ neighborhood_2 }}</span>, <span data-field="neighborhood_3">{{ neighborhood_3 }}</span>, <span data-field="neighborhood_4">{{ neighborhood_4 }}</span>, and <span data-field="neighborhood_5">{{ neighborhood_5 }}</span>). The shuttle operates between 5:00 pm and 1:00 am seven days a week. To request the shuttle from campus, visit the Welcome Center or call 721-588-4018 (calls can be received through WhatsApp).</p>
    </div>
    <div style="flex: 1; padding-left: 20px;">
      <h2 style="font-size: 24px; margin-bottom: 20px;">WELLNESS COUNSELING</h2>
      <p style="line-height: 1.6;">Wellness counseling is available to help students achieve and maintain balance during medical school. Services include individual and group counseling, stress and referral, preventative education, common counseling concerns include homesickness, anxiety, depression, relationship issues, difficulties with cultural adjustment, grief/loss, and academic concerns. The wellness counselor will work with you to access the type of help you need.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-bottom: 40px;">
    <div style="flex: 1; padding-right: 20px;">
      <h2 style="font-size: 24px; margin-bottom: 20px;">FITNESS CENTER</h2>
      <p style="line-height: 1.6;">AUC's fitness center is centrally located and available to campus community members on a 24/7 basis, free of charge. Our open workout area features rubber flooring, state-of-the-art cardio machines, strength training equipment, and weight racks and accessories. Students also enjoy access to two fitness rooms for group exercise, martial arts training, and open gym time.</p>
